codex
The patch enables vector backfill based solely on the stored vector sub-object, which breaks the documented inert semantics for vector declarations without the searchable role when an embedder is live.

Review comment:

- [P2] Restrict vector declarations to searchable roles — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s20c/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/src/lib.rs:17143-17143
  When a caller declares a `vector` sub-object without the `searchable` role, the existing contract treats it as inert-but-round-trippable, but this predicate now treats any `vector_declared = 1` row as enabling the dense arm. In a session with a live embedder, configuring `{roles: [filterable], vector: true}` will therefore enrol/backfill vector kinds and make later writes enqueue embeddings even though that projection is supposed to be inert. The declaration check should include the searchable role (or otherwise use the same active `searchable→vector` predicate) before triggering backfill/late enrolment.
